WEBVTT

00:10.760 --> 00:12.095
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

00:16.016 --> 00:17.642
<i>We are the frontiers</i>

00:21.062 --> 00:22.814
<i>Confront with no fear</i>

00:22.897 --> 00:24.983
<i>From zero to a hundred in an instant</i>

00:25.066 --> 00:27.652
<i>Unveiling mysteries hidden</i>
<i>deep in the dark</i>

00:28.236 --> 00:30.113
<i>Even dead, I rise from the dust</i>

00:30.196 --> 00:32.741
<i>Reaching an unprecedented realm</i>

00:32.824 --> 00:35.035
<i>Trying your uniqueness</i>

00:35.118 --> 00:36.286
<i>It's a test level EX</i>

00:36.369 --> 00:37.662
<i>I'm the best, nothing less</i>

00:37.746 --> 00:40.206
<i>Pioneering from the east to the west</i>

00:40.290 --> 00:42.917
<i>Erasing all who resist, their data and all</i>

00:43.001 --> 00:44.210
<i>Did I really win?</i>

00:44.294 --> 00:45.503
<i>What are these tears?</i>

00:45.587 --> 00:47.922
<i>Who will be hated or loved</i>
<i>by the god of victory?</i>

00:48.006 --> 00:49.215
<i>To Each, their own wishes</i>

00:49.299 --> 00:50.300
<i>With friends, aiming for prize</i>

00:50.383 --> 00:52.343
<i>Seeking answers,</i>
<i>cutting through the unknown</i>

00:52.427 --> 00:53.678
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

00:53.762 --> 00:56.097
<i>Bugged out world, I'm a survivor</i>

00:56.181 --> 00:58.475
<i>Blazing with the guiding fire</i>

00:58.558 --> 01:00.310
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

01:00.393 --> 01:01.436
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

01:01.519 --> 01:02.812
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

01:02.896 --> 01:03.730
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

01:03.813 --> 01:06.691
<i>Declare war. At the system, we aim back</i>

01:06.775 --> 01:09.069
<i>Lose yourself, and it's game over</i>

01:09.152 --> 01:10.987
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

01:11.071 --> 01:11.905
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

01:11.988 --> 01:13.281
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

01:13.364 --> 01:14.699
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

01:18.703 --> 01:20.121
<i>We are the frontiers</i>

01:23.833 --> 01:25.335
<i>Confront with no fear</i>

01:26.252 --> 01:27.462
<i>You know I'll be there</i>

01:27.545 --> 01:28.713
<i>Overturning limits</i>

01:28.797 --> 01:30.507
<i>Now is the new beginning</i>

01:31.508 --> 01:35.428
(Murder At 100 Meters Per Second)

01:35.512 --> 01:40.266
(3 Years Ago
Galaxia Heroes: Burst World Championships)

01:48.858 --> 01:50.902
<i>The strongest pro gamer.</i>

01:51.236 --> 01:53.905
<i>I can finally have a match with you.</i>

01:55.824 --> 01:59.119
<i>I've researched her play style down</i>
<i>to all her minute details.</i>

02:00.036 --> 02:03.540
<i>Her reaction speed is impressive,</i>
<i>I give her that.</i>

02:05.041 --> 02:10.630
<i>But having beaten a lot of pros up</i>
<i>to now, I should be able to deal with it.</i>

02:14.259 --> 02:15.552
Let's have fun.

02:17.345 --> 02:21.724
She acts all chill and playful,
but that ends today!

02:28.314 --> 02:33.069
The new hero from Japan, storming
into the scene with a string of wins, "K,"

02:33.153 --> 02:35.989
picked Armed Lava as expected!

02:36.072 --> 02:41.161
And likewise, the world champion,
Silvia Goldberg, picked Metius!

02:41.244 --> 02:43.663
He knows only a few losses
since his debut!

02:43.746 --> 02:45.373
With his high win rate,

02:45.456 --> 02:49.002
K finally makes his way
into the world championships final!

02:49.085 --> 02:54.924
What kind of battle will he show us
against the world champion?!

02:57.468 --> 03:00.263
Here we go!

03:06.811 --> 03:08.730
Counter grab!

03:09.981 --> 03:12.275
And down against the floor!

03:12.358 --> 03:15.111
<i>Got her! This'll connect to</i>
<i>a Liquid-Metal Bolt strike!</i>

03:15.194 --> 03:16.404
<i>Liquid-Metal-</i>

03:16.487 --> 03:18.448
It connects!

03:18.531 --> 03:22.619
She forced Armed Lava's
impenetrable defense open!

03:23.119 --> 03:24.954
<i>She can do that from that position?</i>

03:30.335 --> 03:31.544
<i>No, it's not over yet!</i>

03:31.628 --> 03:33.796
<i>Gotta observe her movement</i>
<i>and prepare myself again.</i>

03:35.715 --> 03:38.593
Armed Lava's thrown into the air!

03:38.676 --> 03:41.387
There's no stopping this shooting star!

03:45.058 --> 03:47.352
Is this really a human playing?!

03:48.186 --> 03:51.481
<i>No way. This is nothing like</i>
<i>what I saw in videos of her!</i>

03:51.564 --> 03:54.317
<i>This is beyond just about reaction time!</i>

03:54.734 --> 03:59.280
<i>It's like she sees through all my</i>
<i>strategies- every single thing I'd try.</i>

03:59.364 --> 04:01.741
Metius's gauge is maxed out!

04:01.824 --> 04:03.868
The Super Finisher's coming!

04:04.369 --> 04:07.413
Metius Strike!

04:11.042 --> 04:12.877
K.O.!

04:12.961 --> 04:16.047
She nailed it!

04:16.130 --> 04:18.216
The winner is Silvi!

04:18.299 --> 04:22.053
From the moment she broke his guard,
she took him out in an instant!

04:25.431 --> 04:28.393
Th-This is… Silvia's strength…

04:28.476 --> 04:31.020
I never thought I'd be
this helpless against her.

04:31.104 --> 04:32.939
That was amazing!

04:33.022 --> 04:35.525
Good game, K!

04:35.775 --> 04:38.945
I didn't think you'd
take half my health down!

04:39.028 --> 04:41.281
Your fakeouts and strikes are great, too.

04:41.364 --> 04:42.824
Umm…

04:42.907 --> 04:45.243
That was your full name again?

04:46.369 --> 04:49.664
Uomi… Uomi Kei.

04:50.248 --> 04:52.667
I'm Silvia Goldberg.

04:54.168 --> 04:55.795
I know.

04:55.878 --> 04:57.839
I'm not gonna give up, okay?

04:57.922 --> 04:59.257
Silvi.

04:59.757 --> 05:02.302
I will surpass you no matter what!

05:04.262 --> 05:06.848
Great. I can't wait.

05:13.980 --> 05:19.360
So yeah. That was my
first match against Silvia.

05:19.861 --> 05:21.779
What do you think, Sunraku-kun?

05:21.863 --> 05:26.659
We believe you and her
share a similar play style.

05:26.743 --> 05:30.371
Yeah, but she's way faster than me.

05:30.913 --> 05:34.292
She was blocking attacks as if she had a
constant parry success bonus or something.

05:34.375 --> 05:39.630
Her predictions are so precise,
that's just crazy, honestly.

05:40.006 --> 05:43.885
I think I can copy her technique,
but it'd be hard to move exactly like her.

05:44.469 --> 05:46.137
So that's how it is, huh?

05:46.387 --> 05:49.348
If you're only good enough to have an
even match against me playing Metius,

05:49.432 --> 05:51.934
then winning against
Silvia would be impossible.

05:52.018 --> 05:56.689
That's why you said you want to
fight Sunraku-kun "for real," huh?

05:56.773 --> 05:59.942
Sorry I had to hide it from you.

06:00.026 --> 06:02.695
I just don't want you to overthink it.

06:02.779 --> 06:04.322
I'll forgive that.

06:04.405 --> 06:07.075
I did get to kick you
clean in the face, anyway.

06:07.158 --> 06:10.661
Even though it's in VR, it felt
like I'd lose my memory from that.

06:10.745 --> 06:12.997
Anyway, that one doesn't count, okay?

06:13.081 --> 06:14.791
Man, you're stubborn.

06:16.417 --> 06:18.002
After she beat me hard
in our first match,

06:18.086 --> 06:20.379
I put even more effort
into my research on Silvi,

06:20.463 --> 06:24.425
and whenever I find room for improvement,
I switch my character and tactics.

06:24.509 --> 06:29.555
But in official matches, I got
zero wins, eight losses, and a draw.

06:29.639 --> 06:32.517
And Silvia's still evolving even now.

06:35.269 --> 06:36.729
So she beat you up completely.

06:38.147 --> 06:40.650
But you're aiming to win, right?

06:41.275 --> 06:42.652
Of course.

06:43.152 --> 06:45.279
Then we gotta have to do it.

06:45.363 --> 06:49.826
Right when the world is buzzing
all about that Silvi- the Star Rain,

06:50.326 --> 06:54.580
if a rag-tag team like ours can beat them,
wouldn't that be the coolest thing ever?

06:54.956 --> 06:55.957
Yeah!

07:00.711 --> 07:03.881
Katzo seems to be
really enthused about this.

07:03.965 --> 07:08.636
That's how important beating
Silvia is to him, it seems.

07:09.303 --> 07:12.014
<i>Given how determined</i>
<i>Katzo is to fight Silvia,</i>

07:12.098 --> 07:15.852
<i>the rest of us will likely end up</i>
<i>facing those macho dudes.</i>

07:15.935 --> 07:19.355
<i>Better think up ways to beat them, too.</i>

07:19.856 --> 07:22.442
All right! I'm all pumped up!

07:22.525 --> 07:24.610
I'm gonna train hard tonight!

07:27.155 --> 07:30.450
And I'll need some
energy drinks for that, but…

07:31.951 --> 07:34.912
Doesn't seem like they're
selling any imported drinks here.

07:34.996 --> 07:38.332
No, I said coffee!

07:38.416 --> 07:41.419
Dark! A really strong one, and lots of it!

07:41.502 --> 07:45.798
Um, but ma'am,
most coffees are dark, so…

07:45.882 --> 07:50.094
Dark? Yes, that!
Gimme lots of strong ones!

07:51.095 --> 07:53.973
By "dark," maybe she means black coffee?

07:54.056 --> 07:54.891
Black?

07:55.391 --> 07:57.560
Yes, that! Black coffee!

07:58.269 --> 08:01.272
Oh, right. Just one moment, please.

08:02.190 --> 08:04.984
Oh, thanks! Appreciate that, <i>boy</i>!

08:05.067 --> 08:08.196
No, no, no problem at all.

08:09.447 --> 08:10.865
<i>"Boy"?</i>

08:10.948 --> 08:12.909
<i>Is she wearing a disguise?</i>

08:12.992 --> 08:15.453
<i>Is she someone famous?</i>
<i>Looks suspicious.</i>

08:17.622 --> 08:19.790
<i>Not that I'm one to talk, though.</i>

08:19.874 --> 08:20.917
Oh!

08:21.000 --> 08:23.419
That brand! I like it too!

08:23.503 --> 08:25.630
But the ones in Japan are…
a little thin?

08:25.713 --> 08:28.216
Huh? Oh, yes.

08:28.299 --> 08:30.801
They dial down the caffeine over here.

08:36.724 --> 08:38.726
<i>Is this person also a gamer?</i>

08:38.809 --> 08:40.645
Thank you for waiting, ma'am.

08:40.728 --> 08:42.855
Here's the strong black coffee
you asked for.

08:43.731 --> 08:44.774
Wow!

08:44.857 --> 08:48.528
I heard Japan's convenience
store coffee is great,

08:48.611 --> 08:51.280
so I've been waiting for this
moment since forever!

08:51.364 --> 08:54.242
Dark, and lots of it!

08:56.118 --> 08:57.495
Thank you!

09:01.916 --> 09:05.545
It sure is impressive to see someone
get <i>that</i> excited over a coffee, isn't it?.

09:07.380 --> 09:09.507
Wait, that person…

09:11.676 --> 09:13.177
Nah, it can't be.

09:20.977 --> 09:24.105
(That kid sure bought a lot of energy drinks)

09:24.855 --> 09:25.815
(Maybe)

09:26.524 --> 09:28.693
(He's a gamer or something?)

09:34.949 --> 09:36.993
Tasty!

09:39.245 --> 09:42.540
This does deserve a five-star!

09:48.754 --> 09:50.131
Hey there.

09:50.214 --> 09:52.466
<i>What are you doing, Silvi?</i>

09:52.550 --> 09:55.845
<i>Didn't we agree to do a little warm-up</i>
in Galaxia Heroes: Chaos <i>today?</i>

09:55.928 --> 09:57.847
Hmm, sorry.

09:57.930 --> 10:01.851
The jet lag's got me all tired,
so I'm gonna hit the bed early.

10:01.934 --> 10:03.352
Go on without me.

10:03.436 --> 10:05.813
<i>Huh?! Are you kidding me?!</i>

10:05.896 --> 10:07.607
You were so full of energy not so lo-

10:07.690 --> 10:10.443
I'll make up for it tomorrow, okay? Bye.

10:14.864 --> 10:18.117
Well, I'm filled up on caffeine now.

10:18.200 --> 10:20.703
Time to log in right away.

10:22.413 --> 10:27.585
Into that single Japanese game
that broke the entire gaming industry,

10:27.668 --> 10:29.837
<i>Shangri-La Frontier</i>.

10:32.757 --> 10:37.928
Uh, I was thinking about making a plan
to use against those muscle dudes,

10:38.012 --> 10:40.097
but I'm starting to lose my focus.

10:40.431 --> 10:44.018
Compared to the import
drinks Katzo taught me,

10:44.101 --> 10:47.355
this just has, like, no kick.

10:47.855 --> 10:50.691
But drinking two will
get my bladder full…

10:51.359 --> 10:56.030
At a time like this, the best thing to do
is to refresh with other games for a bit,

10:56.113 --> 10:59.992
but I didn't bring my
own VR system with me.

11:08.459 --> 11:10.878
(Shangri-La Frontier Digital Edition)

11:10.961 --> 11:14.382
Found it. <i>SLF</i>'s digital edition!

11:14.465 --> 11:20.513
SLF <i>uses biometrics and</i>
<i>passwords to manage accounts.</i>

11:20.596 --> 11:23.933
<i>As such, you can't make</i>
<i>anything like sub-accounts,</i>

11:24.016 --> 11:28.479
<i>but you can pretty easily access</i>
<i>the game on another device.</i>

11:29.814 --> 11:31.440
<i>Login from another device.</i>

11:31.524 --> 11:34.443
<i>Biometric ID required.</i>

11:36.737 --> 11:37.863
Well…

11:37.947 --> 11:43.494
You know, although they're a different
game, they do share the same system.

11:43.577 --> 11:45.538
It shouldn't be a total waste.

11:45.621 --> 11:47.581
I pause at a pretty nice part, too,

11:47.665 --> 11:51.961
and there are a lot of things
I want to test and check out.

11:52.920 --> 11:55.172
Right! It's settled!
I'll play just for a bit!

11:55.256 --> 11:57.216
I'll play for like an hour tops!

11:57.299 --> 11:58.384
Sorry, Katzo!

11:58.467 --> 12:01.804
I promise I'll just play to refresh
myself and stop right away!

12:08.394 --> 12:10.980
(Login
Ruluiath Empty House)

12:13.107 --> 12:14.984
Hm? Oh, it's you, Sunraku.

12:15.067 --> 12:16.986
Hey, Araba! It's been yesterday.

12:17.528 --> 12:20.614
Hee hee, I'm really logged in.

12:21.782 --> 12:23.993
Looks like Rei hasn't come here yet.

12:26.370 --> 12:29.623
Say, do we have more
furniture here or is it just me?

12:30.166 --> 12:34.420
The human named Akitsuakane
did a lot during the day.

12:34.879 --> 12:36.380
She did?

12:36.464 --> 12:38.924
She did say she could login today,

12:39.008 --> 12:41.469
but of course she won't be up <i>this</i> late.

12:46.098 --> 12:48.767
Guess rabbits aren't nocturnal, huh?

12:50.269 --> 12:51.270
Oh crap!

12:52.188 --> 12:55.441
C'mon, Emul-chan.
Close those eyes, okay?

12:55.524 --> 12:58.527
'Tis time for a nap.

13:01.989 --> 13:02.907
Man, that was close.

13:02.990 --> 13:04.200
If she woke up…

13:04.283 --> 13:07.286
I will join you!

13:08.579 --> 13:10.915
She'd make a lot of noise.

13:11.415 --> 13:13.584
You're going out this late?

13:13.667 --> 13:15.836
I suppose you're the nocturnal one.

13:15.920 --> 13:19.548
When I'm all fired up,
that's when I start moving.

13:19.924 --> 13:22.635
The moment you wake up,
you're on the move.

13:22.718 --> 13:26.764
I know your type. You're like that
fish that dies if it ever stops moving.

13:26.847 --> 13:28.557
Who are you calling a tuna?

13:28.641 --> 13:30.559
You want me to turn you
into a shark-fin soup?

13:30.643 --> 13:32.978
Huh? What is this "shark fin"?

13:33.062 --> 13:34.396
A weapon?

13:34.480 --> 13:37.983
- But he said soup, so is it a dish?
- Well, better go before everyone wakes up.

13:40.986 --> 13:44.990
In <i>SLF</i>, the set of enemies you fight often
changes depending on the time of day.

13:45.074 --> 13:49.203
I was wondering what sort of
changes there are here in Ruluiath.

13:50.704 --> 13:52.456
But would you look at that.

13:52.540 --> 13:55.709
If this city's a ruin
crushed by zombies by day,

13:56.335 --> 14:00.965
then at night, it becomes a
paradise for aquatic life, huh?

14:01.715 --> 14:04.718
Wow! This is quite an awesome view!

14:04.802 --> 14:06.720
I'm not going to stop you now.

14:07.388 --> 14:09.765
But even if it's you,
you better be careful.

14:09.848 --> 14:11.809
Don't let your guard down.

14:11.892 --> 14:12.726
What?

14:13.352 --> 14:16.981
At night, Ruluiath has
a king ruling over it.

14:17.273 --> 14:18.357
A king?

14:27.199 --> 14:29.702
Although it's night,
it's not that dark.

14:29.785 --> 14:33.998
The fishman zombies are back to being
normal fish, so traveling is much easier.

14:34.748 --> 14:37.585
I'm a little curious about this
"king" Araba was talking about.

14:39.545 --> 14:41.839
But for tonight,

14:41.922 --> 14:45.134
I'm gonna examine the mystery
behind Ctarnidd's ability.

14:45.634 --> 14:47.136
The first thing to
check would be…

14:47.636 --> 14:52.057
<i>The crumbled buildings are all fixed</i>
<i>like somebody hit the reset button!</i>

14:52.141 --> 14:54.184
<i>Sunraku-san, what's this?</i>

14:54.268 --> 14:55.561
<i>I don't know.</i>

14:55.644 --> 14:59.899
<i>But if I have to guess, this has to be</i>
<i>another one of Ctarnidd's abilities.</i>

15:00.524 --> 15:05.321
That power that repaired the
destroyed town like it rewinds them back.

15:05.404 --> 15:10.743
But to test that out, I'd need
to break some stuff first.

15:10.826 --> 15:11.660
Hm?

15:12.536 --> 15:15.164
Sometimes the fish exhibit
strange behavior like that.

15:15.748 --> 15:17.166
It must be that.

15:17.249 --> 15:20.836
When you enter the range of Ctarnidd's
"turning" ability from the outside,

15:20.920 --> 15:24.423
you'd get confused because
the directions turned upside down.

15:24.506 --> 15:28.677
To me, this area's filled with air,
but to them, it's filled with water.

15:29.345 --> 15:33.265
But I didn't expect you could also
enter the area directly from outside.

15:33.349 --> 15:36.560
That means this place's not
completely cut off from the outside.

15:36.936 --> 15:41.941
The whole "turned over" city thing is
still a mystery, but more importantly…

15:42.483 --> 15:43.317
Huh?

15:45.319 --> 15:46.862
That guy…

15:46.946 --> 15:49.740
The giga-oarfish I fought yesterday?

15:49.823 --> 15:52.242
He comes in from the outside too?

15:52.326 --> 15:53.994
That's perfect!

15:54.078 --> 15:55.079
He'll do just fine…

15:57.081 --> 15:59.833
What? Another monster?

16:00.626 --> 16:02.169
Blue flame…

16:02.586 --> 16:03.837
It's on fire?

16:04.505 --> 16:06.924
That's an aquatic creature, right?

16:19.395 --> 16:22.481
It took that giga-oarfish on
and it's keeping the fight even.

16:22.564 --> 16:25.985
No, even more. It's totally
the predator in this scenario!

16:30.239 --> 16:33.492
Is that the "king" Araba talked about?

16:52.636 --> 16:55.556
That blue effect… is that electricity?

17:23.625 --> 17:27.254
It insta-killed that giga-oarfish?

17:28.005 --> 17:30.382
A monster with two elements-
blue flame and lighting,

17:30.466 --> 17:34.053
nothing you'd find
from an aquatic animal.

17:34.136 --> 17:37.139
So this is the "king" of the deep sea…!

17:39.475 --> 17:40.726
Sheesh.

17:40.809 --> 17:43.896
A Unique Monster-class enemy
just pops out like it's no big deal.

17:44.271 --> 17:48.400
Once again, Ruluiath is
such a crazy, freaky place.

17:48.859 --> 17:53.906
But as long as this is a game, no way
there are areas that players can't beat.

17:54.323 --> 17:56.784
I'll use that overwhelming
destructive power of yours

17:56.867 --> 17:59.661
as a tool for my experimentation!

18:00.496 --> 18:03.582
If there is something
I don't really like in <i>SLF</i>,

18:03.665 --> 18:05.626
that'd be because of
censorship of graphic content,

18:05.709 --> 18:08.921
the animation for monsters
eating others looks a little iffy.

18:09.379 --> 18:10.881
Hey! You over there!

18:10.964 --> 18:13.675
How long are you gonna keep on
eating, you dual-element orca?!

18:20.474 --> 18:24.436
I heard the Mermen call you a "king."

18:26.438 --> 18:30.943
Will a king smile and let it slide
when his prey gets taken from him?

18:36.448 --> 18:38.951
All right! He took the bait!

18:42.704 --> 18:45.958
<i>How much of this city</i>
<i>you can level to the ground.</i>

18:46.500 --> 18:48.961
<i>And what triggers its repair?</i>

18:52.631 --> 18:54.716
<i>Depending on what I learn</i>
<i>from this experiment,</i>

18:54.800 --> 18:57.219
<i>the way I tackle Ruluiath</i>
<i>would change widely.</i>

18:57.719 --> 19:00.722
I'm gonna have you help me with that,
dual-element orca!

19:05.102 --> 19:08.063
<i>The targets to destroy</i>
<i>are those tall towers</i>

19:08.147 --> 19:11.275
<i>sitting on each corner of the city,</i>
<i>said to be where the "Blockers" are.</i>

19:11.358 --> 19:12.734
<i>A Blocker?</i>

19:12.818 --> 19:17.656
<i>Some bastards with the unique</i>
<i>ability to shut off your powers.</i>

19:17.739 --> 19:21.076
<i>The only one I've heard</i>
<i>about is "Krionaire"</i>

19:21.160 --> 19:24.413
<i>who can seal off</i>
<i>all types of magic.</i>

19:25.414 --> 19:30.043
What happens if I can destroy those
towers where the blockers are?

19:30.127 --> 19:32.671
Don't you wanna find out?

19:35.716 --> 19:39.303
And to do that, I gotta
reach those towers alive!

19:48.145 --> 19:50.439
Those fins you got
flashing with electricity.

19:50.522 --> 19:52.941
It's what you used to kill
of the giga-oafish, huh?

19:53.400 --> 19:56.111
<i>I'm sure that attack deals a lot of damage,</i>

19:56.195 --> 19:59.072
<i>but it took nearly</i>
<i>thirty seconds to activate.</i>

19:59.406 --> 20:02.326
But for someone who'd die
from any form of attack anyway,

20:02.409 --> 20:05.996
that's just a slow-ass attack that
gives me plenty of time to deal with it.

20:06.079 --> 20:08.165
That ain't a threat at all!

20:09.917 --> 20:10.834
<i>It's coming!</i>

20:21.470 --> 20:24.473
The bolts fly around the local area, huh?

20:24.556 --> 20:27.100
Better to think of it as an area attack.

20:50.540 --> 20:53.335
Whoa, did I really dodge that?!

20:53.418 --> 20:57.464
I couldn't launch Inventoria in time at
that distance, I thought I was done for.

20:57.547 --> 21:02.552
Now that's a cutting-edge VR chair people
said to be for commercial use for you.

21:03.095 --> 21:05.055
The response time is
on a whole other level.

21:06.765 --> 21:11.144
There are a lot of benefits to get
from this where your reflex is crucial.

21:14.398 --> 21:17.150
Oops, now's not the time
to marvel at this.

21:17.609 --> 21:19.278
But I can do this!

21:19.361 --> 21:21.154
I just gotta go on to the tower.

21:25.367 --> 21:26.285
What?

21:30.205 --> 21:31.581
A new move?

21:31.665 --> 21:33.458
<i>I better be ready to use Inventoria.</i>

21:53.729 --> 21:55.480
Sunraku-san?!

22:05.615 --> 22:08.744
Lotsa carrots…

22:08.827 --> 22:11.288
So tasty.

22:31.475 --> 22:33.977
I hide in my brain every day

22:34.061 --> 22:35.937
cause I'm running out of patience

22:36.605 --> 22:38.398
lost in distorted thoughts

22:38.482 --> 22:42.277
I can't help but hold my breath

22:42.444 --> 22:44.571
blurred mind, spinning in place

22:44.654 --> 22:46.782
I long to turn away from that scene
to close my eyes.

22:46.865 --> 22:48.033
I don't like what I'm seeing

22:48.116 --> 22:48.950
and it's a curse

22:49.034 --> 22:51.161
it's a thorn in my side

22:52.496 --> 22:54.664
Countless eyes and voices

22:54.748 --> 23:01.463
clapping and laughing,
with a nihilistic air

23:01.546 --> 23:03.632
I'm losing my mind

23:03.715 --> 23:06.176
Inside this scary little world

23:06.259 --> 23:11.056
life is gradually soaking up my dopamine

23:11.139 --> 23:12.516
but I can breathe

23:12.599 --> 23:14.142
I can feel like I matter

23:14.226 --> 23:16.186
in my twisted imagination

23:16.269 --> 23:18.688
cause realitYhurts

23:18.772 --> 23:23.527
I think I'd rather stay here

23:28.573 --> 23:33.453
I think I'd rather stay here

23:43.755 --> 23:47.467
<i>SLF</i> Theater!

23:47.551 --> 23:48.927
Mini!

23:50.220 --> 23:55.225
(Professional Giant Killer's Style)

24:05.235 --> 24:07.070
<i>Arthur Pencilgon.</i>

24:07.154 --> 24:09.656
<i>She's a Player Killer.</i>

24:11.324 --> 24:13.827
<i>She has the monicker of "Giant Killer."</i>

24:14.786 --> 24:19.708
<i>She was the #2 member</i>
<i>of the infamous Asura Kai.</i>

24:19.791 --> 24:23.295
<i>In this episode, we will</i>
<i>look into her style of PK.</i>

24:24.504 --> 24:27.340
<i>Giant Killer's style #1.</i>

24:27.424 --> 24:28.758
<i>Use trap.</i>

24:28.842 --> 24:33.013
Um, excuse me,
I got stuck in the mud.

24:33.096 --> 24:35.307
Would you please help me?

24:36.141 --> 24:37.601
You must have had a tough time, huh?

24:37.684 --> 24:40.812
We're coming. Just wait over there.

24:47.652 --> 24:48.612
There.

24:49.279 --> 24:51.948
<i>Giant Killer's style #2.</i>

24:52.032 --> 24:53.533
Target solo player.

24:53.617 --> 24:55.493
Thanks for the help today.

24:55.577 --> 24:57.454
I'm done for today now.

24:57.537 --> 24:58.371
Good work.

24:58.455 --> 25:00.916
See you. Feel free to hit me up anytime.

25:06.421 --> 25:07.547
Huh?

25:07.631 --> 25:08.798
Good work.

25:13.011 --> 25:16.932
As a human, I gotta use my head if I'm
going to fight someone stronger than me.

25:17.390 --> 25:21.019
Unlike some fussy gamer
or sexually ambiguous gamer,

25:21.102 --> 25:22.854
I actually know how to use my brain.

25:30.946 --> 25:34.574
How dare you do that to us!

25:34.658 --> 25:40.956
Looks like the gamers I've killed flock
together to enact their revenge on me.

25:41.039 --> 25:45.085
<i>No matter what scheme she has</i>
<i>up her sleeve, it's one against many.</i>

25:45.168 --> 25:47.754
<i>Just what can she do?</i>

25:48.463 --> 25:49.756
At a time like this…

25:49.839 --> 25:50.966
<i>Like this?</i>

25:51.049 --> 25:54.302
The final Giant Killer's style!

25:54.386 --> 25:56.554
I'll take everyone down with me!

25:56.638 --> 25:57.472
<i>Huh?</i>

25:57.806 --> 25:58.932
Self-destruct.

25:59.015 --> 26:02.936
(Self-destruct)

26:06.273 --> 26:08.817
Aah, that was fun.
